## Backend — tts_server.py (FastAPI, port 8765)

### Dual-mode architecture (laptop + Kaggle GPU)
The laptop server always runs (port 8765). Heavy ML work routes to a **Kaggle GPU
notebook** via cloudflared tunnel when `KAGGLE_ENABLED=true`. When Kaggle is off,
unreachable, or hours are spent, **everything falls back to local CPU** automatically.

| Workload | Kaggle on (`*_PROVIDER=kaggle`) | Local fallback |
|----------|----------------------------------|----------------|
| PDF layout (`/page_layout`) | Kaggle CPU (pdfplumber + PyMuPDF) | `page_layout_service.py` |
| Slide analysis (`/analyze`) | Qwen **7B** on GPU (llama-cpp) | Local Qwen **3B** via `LLMState` |
| Telugu translation | NLLB-600M on GPU | Local NLLB-1.3B |
| Decorative image gen | Kaggle SDXL (Layer 1+2) via tunnel | Lanczos fallback (no local GPU gen) |
| Image upscale (informational) | **Always laptop** (Lanczos) | Same — `upscale_service.py` on CPU |
| TTS / karaoke | Always laptop | Sarvam → edge-tts fallback |

Kaggle server: `server/kaggle/veda_gpu_server.py` — endpoints `/health`, `/upload_pdf`,
`/page_layout`, `/analyze`, `/translate`, `/generate_prompt`, `/generate_image`.
**No `/upscale_image` on Kaggle** — laptop orchestrates; decorative images call Kaggle gen via
`kaggle_generate_image()` from `/upscale_image`. Informational images stay Lanczos on laptop.
Tunnel URL changes each notebook session; update `KAGGLE_API_BASE_URL` in `.env` and **save the file**
before restarting the backend. `load_dotenv(..., override=True)` so `.env` wins over stale shell env.

**Kaggle GPU pinning (T4 x2):** Qwen 7B + SmolVLM → GPU 0 (`main_gpu=0`); NLLB-600M + SDXL → `cuda:1`
(env `NLLB_DEVICE`). **Sequential pre-warm** at startup: NLLB → Qwen → SmolVLM → SDXL (see below).

**Kaggle notebook secrets (recommended):**
| Secret | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `HF_TOKEN` | HuggingFace Read token — faster downloads, avoids rate-limit stalls |
| `KAGGLE_API_SECRET` | Set in Cell 2 env (must match laptop `server/.env`) |

**Kaggle notebook workflow:**
1. Publish bundle: `server\kaggle\prepare_kaggle_dataset.bat` → `publish_kaggle_dataset.bat`
2. Attach dataset `project-models` (**latest version**) — user slug e.g. `eakeswar/project-models`
3. Settings: GPU T4 x2, Internet ON
4. Add-ons → Secrets → `HF_TOKEN` = HuggingFace Read token (`hf_...`)
5. **Cell 1:** copy from dataset to `/kaggle/working/`: `veda_gpu_server.py`, `security.py`,
   `qwen_config.py`, `analyze_prompts.py`, `page_layout_service.py`, `image_gen_service.py`
   (do **not** copy `upscale_service.py` / `rrdb_net.py` — removed with Real-ESRGAN)
6. **Cell 2:** load `HF_TOKEN` via `UserSecretsClient`, set `HF_HOME` + `HUGGING_FACE_HUB_CACHE` to
   `/kaggle/working/hf_cache` (persists downloads across re-runs — do not "Restart & Clear All"),
   `VEDA_QUIET=0`, `KAGGLE_API_SECRET`, run server. Default img2img is `segmind/SSD-1B` (no env needed).
7. **Wait for pre-warm** (`all model pre-warm complete`) — first run ~7–15 min with SSD-1B; **do not cancel**
   Warm re-runs with HF cache in working: ~2–4 min
8. Copy tunnel URL to laptop `server/.env` → restart backend
9. Keep notebook running; stop session when done (GPU hours tick while open)

**Two different Kaggle credentials:**
| Credential | Purpose |
|------------|---------|
| `KAGGLE_API_TOKEN` + `KAGGLE_USERNAME` | Official Kaggle API — publish `project-models` from laptop |
| `KAGGLE_API_SECRET` | Custom tunnel password between laptop ↔ GPU notebook (required, no default) |

### API Endpoints
| Method | Path | What it does |
|--------|------|--------------|
| GET | /health | Health check + provider modes + Kaggle reachability (tunnel URL redacted) |
| POST | /upload_pdf | Saves active_doc.pdf; mirrors bytes to Kaggle when layout provider is Kaggle |
| GET | /page_layout?page=N | Returns { width, height, lines[], images[] } — Kaggle or local |
| POST | /analyze | Slide JSON via Kaggle 7B or local 3B; accepts `page_layout` (plain/structured/qa) |
| POST | /translate | String list translation — Kaggle or local NLLB, Sarvam fallback |
| POST | /translate_deck | Full deck Telugu — uses `translate_strings_for_deck()` (Kaggle-aware) |
| POST | /translate_fields | Lazy secondary-field translation — Kaggle-aware |
| POST | /tts | Sarvam TTS → returns { audio, word_boundaries[] }; edge-tts fallback |
| GET | /tts_stream | Streams audio (Sarvam or edge-tts fallback) |
| POST | /tts_boundaries | Returns only word_boundaries (no audio) |
| POST | /transcribe | OpenAI Whisper STT → returns { text, word_boundaries[] } |
| POST | /upscale_image | Tiny decorative → Kaggle SDXL img2img; informational/large decorative → Lanczos on laptop |

### Key Classes & Functions
- `security.py` — `validate_pdf_bytes()`, `require_kaggle_secret()`, `cors_origins()`, payload limits
- `qwen_config.py` — `get_local_qwen_gguf_info()` (3B default), `get_kaggle_qwen_gguf_info()` (7B default)
- `SarvamMemoryCache` — in-memory single-entry cache (text+lang+voice+rate as key)
- `LLMState` — singleton for llama-cpp Qwen (local fallback only)
- `IndicTransState` — singleton for NLLB-200-1.3B (local fallback translation)
- `PDFMetadataAnalyzer` — in `page_layout_service.py`; header/footer detection
- `extract_page_layout()` — in `page_layout_service.py`; shared by laptop + Kaggle
- `upscale_image()` — in `upscale_service.py`; Lanczos-only, laptop only
- `build_analyze_messages()` / `extract_analysis_json()` — in `analyze_prompts.py`
- `run_semantic_analysis()` — routes `/analyze` to Kaggle or `analyze_text_semantic_local()`
- `translate_strings_for_deck()` — Kaggle-first; falls back to local NLLB if Kaggle fails
- `kaggle_client` — `should_use_kaggle()`, `kaggle_analyze()`, `kaggle_translate()`,
  `kaggle_page_layout()`, `kaggle_upload_pdf()`, `kaggle_generate_prompt()`, `kaggle_generate_image()`
- `decorative_image.is_decorative_image()` / `is_tiny_image()` — decorative + size gate before image gen
- `image_gen_service.run_layer1()` / `run_full_pipeline()` — Kaggle-only (SmolVLM + Qwen + SDXL)
- `detect_speech_boundaries(wav_bytes)` — finds lead-in/lead-out silence in WAV
- `adjust_boundaries_to_silence(boundaries, wav_bytes)` — corrects STT timestamps
- `generate_fallback_boundaries(text, duration)` — proportional fallback if STT fails
- `translate_strings_indictrans2()` — local NLLB only (fallback path)
- `translate_strings_sarvam()` — Sarvam Translate API (last-resort fallback)

### LLM Config
- **Primary (when Kaggle on):** Qwen 2.5-**7B**-Instruct GGUF (`qwen2.5-7b-instruct-q3_k_m.gguf`, ~3.8 GB)
  on Kaggle GPU via llama-cpp (`n_gpu_layers=-1`). Controlled by `KAGGLE_LLM_SIZE=7B`.
  Note: single-file **q3_k_m** used because q4_k_m 7B is split into 2 shards on HuggingFace.
- **Fallback (laptop):** Qwen 2.5-**3B**-Instruct GGUF on CPU via `LLMState`. Controlled by `LOCAL_LLM_SIZE=3B`.
- Loaded via llama-cpp-python with n_ctx=4096, n_threads=min(8, cpu_count) on laptop
- JSON auto-repair in `analyze_prompts.extract_analysis_json()` (small models produce malformed JSON)
- Auto-downloads GGUF from HuggingFace on first local /analyze if not in server/models/
- Download 7B for bundle: `python server/kaggle/download_qwen_7b.py`

### Translation (NLLB-200)
- **Kaggle (primary when notebook up):** facebook/nllb-200-distilled-600M on `cuda:1`
  via `run_nllb_translate()` — batched (default 4), `max_new_tokens`, pre-warm on startup
- **Laptop fallback:** facebook/nllb-200-1.3B on CPU via `IndicTransState`
  (auto-used when Kaggle tunnel is down or `/translate` returns 500/530)
- Language code map (INDICTRANS_LANG_MAP): te-IN → tel_Telu, hi-IN → hin_Deva, etc.
- All user-facing translation goes through `translate_strings_for_deck()` (Kaggle-first)
- Sarvam Translate API is last-resort fallback only (requires valid `SARVAM_API_KEY`)

### Image upscaling & decorative AI generation (Jul 10 2026)
**Informational images** (charts, screenshots, text-heavy) always use **Lanczos on laptop CPU**
via `upscale_service.py` (YuNet/HOG people-aware routing). Real-ESRGAN remains removed.

**Decorative images** (covers, illustrations, generic photos) route through a **2-layer Kaggle pipeline**
when `IMAGE_GEN_PROVIDER=auto|kaggle` and Kaggle is reachable; any failure silently falls back to Lanczos.

#### Layer 1 — prompt building (cuda:0, shared with Qwen 7B)
- **SmolVLM-500M-Instruct** (`HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM-500M-Instruct`) captions the source image
- **Qwen 7B** (already loaded via `get_llm()`) refines caption + page text → SDXL prompt
- Endpoint: `POST /generate_prompt` (debug — no image output)

#### Layer 2 — generation (cuda:1, shares GPU with NLLB-600M)
- **SSD-1B img2img** `segmind/SSD-1B` (default; SDXL-architecture, ~3 GB, ~60% faster than base SDXL)
- Override: `SDXL_MODEL=stabilityai/stable-diffusion-xl-base-1.0` (~6 GB) or `segmind/Segmind-Vega` (~2 GB)
- Uses **original PDF image as init image** with low denoising strength (`SDXL_STRENGTH` ~0.35)
- Output clamped 512–1024px, multiple of 8; VRAM-aware max side (768 or 1024)
- Negative prompt: text, watermark, logo, words, changed composition, etc.
- Endpoint: `POST /generate_image` → `{ caption, prompt, image, width, height, method }`
- Method: `layer2_smolvlm_qwen_ssd1b_img2img` / `ssd1b_img2img` (or `sdxl_img2img` when using base SDXL)

#### Laptop routing (`tts_server.py` `/upscale_image`)
- `decorative_image.is_decorative_image()` using `overlapWordCount` + page metadata from layout
- **Size gate**: only **tiny** decorative images (`w < 400` or `h < 400`) → Kaggle img2img
- Larger decorative images → Lanczos (already decent size)
- Frontend passes `page_text`, `page_width`, `page_height`, `image_meta`, `is_image_primary` via `upscaleImages()`
- `kaggle_generate_image()` on decorative+tiny; Lanczos on informational, large decorative, or Kaggle failure

#### Decorative vs informational (`decorative_image.py` + `overlapWordCount`)
- `page_layout_service.py` adds `overlapWordCount` per image (pdfplumber words overlapping bbox > 45%)
- Conservative default: uncertain → Lanczos
- Decorative: `is_image_primary` pages, or inset photo with `overlapWordCount < 3` and normal aspect/area
- Informational: `overlapWordCount >= 8`, screenshot/chart patterns

#### Kaggle runtime deps (NOT in server/vendor/)
- `diffusers`, `accelerate`, `safetensors` — pip-installed at Kaggle notebook startup
- `transformers` pinned `>=4.46.2,<4.49` + `huggingface_hub>=0.34,<1.0` (see problems below)

#### Lanczos routing table (informational path — unchanged)

| Condition | Method | Response `method` field |
|-----------|--------|-------------------------|
| People detected, tiny (< 400px either dim) | Lanczos ×4 + Unsharp Mask | `lanczos_people_x4` |
| People detected, normal size | Lanczos ×2 + Unsharp Mask | `lanczos_people_x2` |
| No people, tiny | Lanczos ×4 + Unsharp Mask | `lanczos_x4` |
| No people, normal size | Lanczos ×2 + Unsharp Mask | `lanczos_x2` |

- Face model: `server/data/face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx` (~230 KB)
- If YuNet missing, conservatively uses Lanczos (no ESRGAN fallback)
- `UPSCALE_PROVIDER=local` always for Lanczos execution; decorative gen uses `IMAGE_GEN_PROVIDER`
- Legacy `RealESRGAN_x4plus.pth` / `rrdb_net.py` may remain in server/models/ but are unused

### Text + Image Extraction (/page_layout)
- Logic lives in `page_layout_service.extract_page_layout()` — used by laptop and Kaggle
- **Text**: pdfplumber with column detection + image-zone filtering; PyMuPDF fallback
  - Column-aware reading order: gutter ≥ 3% page width → 2-column layout
  - Primary column = more words first; secondary column (sidebar) last
  - Image-zone filtering: words overlapping **inset** images by > 45% of word width dropped
  - Background-like images (>85% page dim or >45% page area) excluded from overlap filter
  - Header/footer filtering via `PDFMetadataAnalyzer`
- **Images**: PyMuPDF `get_images(full=True)` + `get_image_rects(xref)`
  - Filters: skip w/h < 5, skip w/h < 50 (icons), skip w > 90% page width (backgrounds)
  - Each image includes `overlapWordCount` (words overlapping image zone via pdfplumber)
- When `LAYOUT_PROVIDER=kaggle`: PDF mirrored to Kaggle on upload; layout fetched from tunnel

### Phase 1 magazine layout (Jul 8 2026) — frontend + LLM input
Raw `/page_layout` lines are post-processed in `pdfUtils.js` before slide build and `/analyze`:
- `mergeStackedHeadlineLines()` — merges multi-line magazine titles (e.g. "IS IT REALLY TRUE THAT …"
  + "… stars are twinkling?")
- `collapsePartialDuplicateLines()` — removes substring-duplicate title fragments
- `buildStructuredAnalyzeText()` — tags lines `[HEADLINE]`, `[SUBHEAD]`, `[BODY]`, `[CALLOUT]`
- `detectCalloutPage()` — Q&A / "Did you know?" magazine callout detection → `page_layout: "qa"`
- Deck carries `analyzeText` + `pageLayout`; `fetchSemanticAnalysis()` sends these to `/analyze`
- `analyze_prompts.build_analyze_messages()` understands structured/qa layouts (merge headlines,
  use BODY for summary/highlights)
- **Not yet built:** GPU vision parser (Docling/Marker) for hardest decorative layouts (Phase 2)

### Known Issues / Things to Watch
1. SarvamMemoryCache is single-entry only — second unique request evicts the first
2. /transcribe uses OpenAI Whisper API (costs money) — Sarvam STT used for karaoke instead
3. CORS restricted to localhost dev origins via `VEDA_CORS_ORIGINS` (not `*` in production path)
4. Kaggle tunnel URL (`trycloudflare.com`) changes every notebook restart — update `.env`
   and **save file** (`Ctrl+S`) before restarting backend; stale shell env vars are overridden
5. Kaggle GPU quota: 30 h/week; session must stay open while using Kaggle providers
6. When `KAGGLE_ENABLED=false`, all providers fall back to laptop CPU automatically
7. Laptop still loads local Qwen/NLLB on fallback paths — heavy RAM when Kaggle is off
8. LLMState on laptop is CPU only (no GPU on Windows server)
9. `SARVAM_API_KEY` placeholder causes 403 — TTS falls back to edge-tts; translate falls
   back to local NLLB if Kaggle also fails
10. Cloudflare 530 = Kaggle notebook stopped or tunnel dead — restart notebook, new URL;
    set `KAGGLE_ENABLED=false` temporarily to use laptop-only while notebook is down
11. `KAGGLE_API_SECRET` must be strong (≥16 chars) — default `veda-kaggle-dev` is rejected
12. After republishing `project-models`, re-attach **latest version** in notebook and re-run cells
13. Magazine callout pages (Discovery Q&A spreads) may still need Phase 2 GPU layout parser
14. SDXL img2img fidelity depends on `SDXL_STRENGTH` — tune 0.25–0.45 if output still drifts
15. Only **tiny decorative** images get SDXL — larger decorative use Lanczos; many photos stay informational due to `overlapWordCount`
16. **First Kaggle session pre-warm ~7–15 min** (SSD-1B ~3 GB vs old SDXL ~6 GB); set `HF_TOKEN`,
    `HF_HOME=/kaggle/working/hf_cache`, `VEDA_QUIET=0`, do not cancel. Warm re-run ~2–4 min.
17. **Cloudflare 524** on image-gen if pre-warm incomplete — wait for `image_gen_prewarm: true` in Kaggle `/health`
18. `/generate_prompt` and `/generate_image` return **503** while `prewarm_in_progress` — laptop falls back to Lanczos
19. Kaggle `/health` (GPU server): `prewarm_step`, `prewarm_in_progress`, `image_gen_prewarm`, `nllb_loaded`, `llm_loaded`

