## Environment Variables (.env)
```
SARVAM_API_KEY=your_key_here
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key_here   # Optional, only for /transcribe endpoint
# VEDA_API_KEY=...             # Optional — require auth on laptop server
# VEDA_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173

LOCAL_LLM_SIZE=3B              # Laptop CPU fallback: 0.5B / 1.5B / 3B
KAGGLE_LLM_SIZE=7B             # Kaggle GPU: 7B (q3_k_m in project-models bundle)

# Kaggle GPU tunnel — set KAGGLE_ENABLED=true only while notebook session is running
KAGGLE_ENABLED=false
KAGGLE_API_BASE_URL=https://xxxx.trycloudflare.com
KAGGLE_API_SECRET=             # Strong random secret (required; no veda-kaggle-dev)
KAGGLE_API_TIMEOUT=120

# Provider routing: local | kaggle | auto
LLM_PROVIDER=local
TRANSLATE_PROVIDER=local
LAYOUT_PROVIDER=local
UPSCALE_PROVIDER=local         # Lanczos execution always on laptop CPU
IMAGE_GEN_PROVIDER=auto        # auto|kaggle|local — decorative SDXL routing (local = Lanczos only)
# IMAGE_GEN_PREWARM=1          # Kaggle: sequential model pre-load at startup (default on)
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...              # Kaggle notebook secret only — not laptop .env
# SDXL_STRENGTH=0.35           # img2img denoising (0.25–0.45 faithful)
# SDXL_MODEL=segmind/SSD-1B      # default img2img (~3 GB); override: stabilityai/stable-diffusion-xl-base-1.0

# Kaggle official API — publish project-models from laptop
KAGGLE_USERNAME=your_username
KAGGLE_API_TOKEN=KGAT_...      # kaggle.com/settings/api
KAGGLE_DATASET_SLUG=project-models
```
When Kaggle hours are spent or tunnel is dead: set `KAGGLE_ENABLED=false` (or stop notebook) —
providers use laptop fallback without code changes.
`tts_server.py` uses `load_dotenv(..., override=True)` so saved `.env` always wins
over stale shell environment variables.

---

## Installed Dependencies (server/vendor/)
- fastapi, uvicorn, edge-tts — core backend
- pymupdf (fitz) — PDF parsing + image extraction
- pdfplumber, pdfminer.six — layout-aware text extraction (column detection, image-zone filtering)
  - cryptography + cffi installed system-wide (not in vendor) — required by pdfminer.six
- llama-cpp-python — local LLM inference
- torch (CPU build) — required for NLLB-200 translation (local fallback)
- transformers, sentencepiece, sacremoses — NLLB-200 model loading and tokenization
- Pillow, opencv-python-headless — image processing for /upscale_image (Lanczos + YuNet/HOG)
- requests, python-dotenv, httpx — HTTP and config
- elevenlabs, openai — optional TTS/STT alternatives

